{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 20.66,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c): refer driver DRV-09851 to driver-conduct review — a repeat-deviation pattern is established on driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 3 (POL-RD-06) and the deviation on this trip is MATERIAL (60.0%, POL-RD-01). The review rides with this ruling and does not delay or displace the refund."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 20.66 charged for trip TRP-02851 is refunded in full to the rider, and the case is sent for driver-conduct review. Why, step by step.\n\n1. The detour is proved, and it is a material one. The distance that governs is the GPS trace EV-GPS-02851 — 14.4 km — and not the rounded convenience copy on the trip record, because POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure govern. The booked optimal route on EV-TRIP-02851 is 9.0 km. The excess is 5.4 km, or 60.0% of optimal: above both POL-RD-01 gates (0.8 km and 20%) and above the 50% that makes the deviation MATERIAL. The trace is clean for policy purposes — 114 fixes at 10-second intervals, maximum gap 0.0 s, empty gaps list, 100% coverage — so POL-RD-07(a) to (c) do not fire and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. The rider's burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged: the trip id TRP-02851 matches across EV-TRIP-02851, EV-GPS-02851 and EV-FARE-02851, and the excess is measured from an unimpaired trace.\n\n2. Nothing reduces the excess. The chat log EV-CHAT-02851 holds 0 messages, so there is no rider-requested detour (POL-RD-04); no pickup or dropoff amendment was made (POL-RD-05); the vehicle was RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL (POL-RD-12). The driver's explanation, 'Road works.', names no advisory evidence ID, and no traffic advisory is on file: EV-ADVIS-02851-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. That artifact carries no fact and its absence is all it evidences; it discounts nothing here. Without a record naming a road the optimal route traverses, a validity window and an alternative-route length, POL-RD-03 cannot be run, so the traffic assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08 and under POL-RD-13 the deviation stands at the measured figure. The assertion is discarded and no advisory was on file. The driver's escalation argument is rejected on the same ground: a bare traffic assertion that names no advisory as its support is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so the POL-RD-10(5) trigger is not engaged, and no other trigger of POL-RD-10 fires — identifiers match, timestamps do not disagree, the trace is not impaired, and the refund is inside both the SGD 150.00 and charged_total limits.\n\n3. The arithmetic, on the booked optimal route. EV-FARE-02851 records fare_model METERED and quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not apply and POL-RD-02 does. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 9.0 + 0.28 x 13.0) x 1.0 surge, read from the FARE_BREAKDOWN, where the clause places it) + 0.80 platform fee = SGD 14.99. charged_total = SGD 20.66. POL-RD-02 refund = 20.66 - 14.99 = SGD 5.67, payable SGD 5.70. The ERP and toll lines are 0.00, there is no airport surcharge (the trip neither starts nor ends at an airport), waiting_time_fee is 0.0 and promo_discount is 0.0, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing on top and nothing is subtracted.\n\n4. The uplift, with both figures side by side. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d on EV-DPROF-02851 is 3, which meets POL-RD-06's threshold of '3 or more'; the test is disjunctive, so the ratio limb (3/180 = 1.7%) need not be met, and the driver's argument that only the absolute limb may be used does not alter the clause, which sets the floor at 3 and gives no discretion. Because the deviation is MATERIAL and substantiated on this trip's own trace, POL-RD-06(b) licenses FULL_REFUND of charged_total: the POL-RD-02 figure is SGD 5.70 and the uplifted figure is SGD 20.66 — an uplift of SGD 14.96. There are no government-set or third-party pass-through lines to carve out. I have used only deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d for this test; prior_deviation_flags and every other profile field are context only under POL-GEN-01 and played no part.\n\n5. Referral. POL-RD-06(c) requires the conduct referral set out above; a referral never suppresses the money, so the refund issues regardless.\n\nThe refund of SGD 20.66 is above the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so this ruling issues but the amount is held for release by the human queue. Either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
