    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. The trip booked at 9.0 km was driven as 14.4 km, and the whole contested charge of SGD 20.66 is returned to the rider.\n\n1. The deviation is established on this trip's own evidence. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing measure, and EV-GPS-02851 records 14.4 km, against the platform optimal route of 9.0 km stored at booking on EV-TRIP-02851. The excess is 5.4 km, 60.0% of optimal, so both gates pass (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km), and the excess also clears the 50% materiality gate. The trace is clean for policy purposes: 114 fixes at a 10-second sampling interval, 100% coverage, an empty gaps list and max_gap_sec of 0.0, so none of POL-RD-07(a)–(c) fires, the trace is not impaired, and the rider's POL-RD-08(b) burden is discharged from the trace itself.\n\n2. The driver's 'Road works' explanation does not reduce the excess. EV-ADVIS-02851-01 is MISSING — no payload, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT (the driver disclosed that impairment, and I record it) — so POL-RD-03 cannot be run: there is no advisory naming a road the optimal route traverses, no validity window and no alternative-route distance. Under POL-RD-08 an assertion that cites no evidence ID carries no weight and is discarded, and under POL-RD-13(1) the driver's statement, which names no advisory for its excuse, is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) does not fire. The driver's separate argument that naming the absent advisory's identifier triggers POL-RD-10(5) is rejected: the asserting party cited no advisory in support of the excuse — the driver's own claim concedes POL-RD-03 cannot be run at all — so no exculpatory clause rests on a cited artifact, and the absence is recorded and citable without holding the money. POL-RD-13(2) therefore applies and the deviation stands at the measured figure.\n\n3. No other exoneration or adjustment applies. EV-CHAT-02851 is complete with 0 messages, so there is no POL-RD-04 rider instruction and no chat_message.waypoint_hint to test; pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 cannot run and no substitute re-quote may be derived; vehicle_type is RYDE_X and solo_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-12 has no work to do; and fare_model is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not close the distance remedy. The booked 9.0 km optimal route is the baseline.\n\n4. The POL-RD-02 arithmetic, for the record: recomputed_fare = (SGD 3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 9.0 km + 0.28 x 13.0 min) x a 1.0 surge multiplier, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier where POL-RD-02 places it, + SGD 0.80 platform fee + no ERP, tolls or surcharges + SGD 0.00 waiting time - SGD 0.00 promo discount = SGD 14.99. charged_total = SGD 20.66, so the refund is 20.66 - 14.99 = SGD 5.67, rounded up to SGD 5.70. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and 27.4% of the charge, so a POL-RD-02 partial refund would be SGD 5.70.\n\n5. But the remedy is uplifted, so SGD 5.70 is not the outcome. The deviation is MATERIAL (60.0% against the 50.0% gate), so the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is required, and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 3, which meets the clause's '3 or more' limb. The alternative ratio limb (3 / 180 = 1.67%) is not needed, because the clause states the two limbs disjunctively; the driver's argument that the uplift should be refused because the count sits at the clause's floor is rejected on the clause's own words. A repeat deviation pattern is therefore ESTABLISHED, and because this trip's deviation is both material and substantiated on its own evidence, POL-RD-06(b) licenses FULL_REFUND of charged_total rather than the POL-RD-02 partial. The two figures side by side, as the clause requires: POL-RD-02 partial = SGD 5.70; POL-RD-06(b) uplifted = SGD 20.66. No government-set or third-party pass-through line is uplifted and none exists here: erp_gantries is empty with an ERP total of SGD 0.00, there is no airport surcharge (this trip neither originates nor ends at an airport), waiting_time_fee is SGD 0.00 and promo_discount is SGD 0.00, so nothing is carved out and there is no billing-integrity line under POL-RD-09(4) for a referral. On POL-GEN-01 I use only deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d for that test; prior_deviation_flags (5) is a lifetime counter and is not used.\n\n6. Outcome and referral. The rider is the filing party, payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.0, so the refund of SGD 20.66 moves the contested amount back to the rider. Under POL-RD-06(c) the case is additionally referred to driver-conduct review; that referral rides with the money and does not delay it. POL-GEN-03 confirms a referral never suppresses the monetary ruling.\n\n7. The monetary effect, SGD 20.66, exceeds the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so the refund is issued but held for release by a human reviewer rather than executed automatically; that is a POL-GEN-05 hold, not an escalation.\n\nConfidence: 0.90. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact — the GPS trace, the trip record, the fare breakdown and the driver profile — has weight_multiplier 1.0, and the absent advisory can carry no fact and therefore does not cap confidence. This ruling was made without human review; either party may appeal it under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "No escalation trigger fires and the rider asks the Judge to rule on the money rather than hold it. The trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; no timestamps run backwards or disagree; the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c), so POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged; and the POL-RD-02 refund of 5.67 is far below SGD 150.00 and below charged_total, so POL-RD-10(6) is not engaged. POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged either, because the driver cited no advisory identifier at all: under POL-RD-13(1) an assertion that cites no artifact cannot be invoked against one, and the absence of an advisory no party has cited is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction in it.",
      "side": "RIDER",
